# CoW true-lazy P3 tier-1 — control-flow-NESTED mutation witness.
#
# `String x = coll.get(0).unwrap()` then a mutation of `coll` (`fill`,
# which reallocs the element storage) buried inside an `if` branch. The
# forward-scan is CONSTRUCT-AGNOSTIC: it recurses through the `if` body and
# sees the `coll.fill(...)` mutation, so the source root `coll` is marked
# mutated and the bind does NOT flip — `x` eager-clones BEFORE the loop, so
# the post-`if` reads observe the PRE-mutation value. This is the correct
# tier-1 outcome: the whole-function scan over-clones (it can't tell the
# mutation is gated behind a runtime-false condition) but is always sound —
# an under-clone here would dangle `x` into the realloc'd buffer (UAF).
void main():
    Vector[String] coll = ["alphalonglonglongstring", "betalonglonglongstring"]
    String x = coll.get(0).unwrap()
    bool grow = true
    if grow:
        coll.fill(4, "z")
        coll.fill(4, "newlonglonglonglonglonglonglonglongstringhere")
    print(x)
    print(x.len())
